# Copilot for Finance: Student Prompt Handout 

Empower your workforce with Microsoft 365 Copilot Use Cases · Finance (Data Analysis) 

Use this handout to follow along during the session and to try every prompt again afterwards. Each prompt is shown exactly as it is used in class, grouped by demo and by the app you run it in. Copy a prompt, paste it into Copilot, then review and refine the answer. 

The scenario 

You are on Rita Chen's regional finance team at Meridian Car Rental, a company that rents cars at 40 airports and is spending $48 million to switch 12 airport fleets to electric vehicles (EVs). Over Thanksgiving weekend, most of the chargers at Denver stopped working: customers waited up to two hours and 340 walked away. To keep customers moving, Meridian paid for partner cars, gas cars driven in from other cities, mobile charging trucks, overtime and customer compensation. The charging company may owe some of it back, but maybe not all. It is Monday morning and the steering committee meets Friday, including a decision on Phoenix. Your job: say what the weekend really cost, what can be recovered, where the budget stands, and what each Phoenix option is worth, with numbers you can defend. 

